From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rmxunet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 19:14:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/ps4: add Aeolia/Belize fan threshold and RPM hwmon
 driver

Adds ps4-fan.c and ps4-fan.h, a Linux hwmon driver for the PS4 fan
controller on Aeolia (CXD90025G) and Belize southbridges.

Exposes three hwmon attributes under /sys/class/hwmon/hwmonX/:
  temp1_input  (RO) - live APU temperature in milli-Celsius
                      source: ICC 0x0B/0x01 reply[3], plain u8 Celsius
  temp1_crit   (RW) - fan threshold in milli-Celsius (45000-85000)
                      read:  ICC 0x0A/0x07 reply[5]
                      write: read-modify-write via 0x0A/0x07 -> 0x0A/0x06
  fan1_input   (RO) - fan speed in RPM
                      source: ICC 0x0A/0x08 reply[8:12], u32 LE 16.16
                      fixed-point, divide by 65536

The fan threshold write implements a full read-modify-write cycle.
The EMC thermal config struct (0x0A/0x07) contains factory PID flags
at bytes [9]=0x08 and [12]=0x80 that must be preserved. Sending a
zero-filled payload destroys these flags, disabling the EMC PID loop
and causing fan RPM to read 0 until hard power cycle. This was the
bug in the legacy ps4fancontrol userspace tool (6-byte alloc, 52-byte
length passed to ioctl, random kernel stack injected into EMC config).

Register map confirmed via live hardware probing on Aeolia PHAT:
  0x0A/0x08 reply[8:12]: RPM as u32 LE 16.16 fixed-point
  0x0A/0x08 reply[16:18]: APU temp as u16 LE 8.8 fixed-point
  0x0B/0x01 reply[3]: APU temp as plain u8 integer Celsius

Compatible with lm_sensors, fancontrol, and any hwmon-aware tool.

Signed-off-by: rmux <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
---
 drivers/ps4/Makefile  |  10 +-
 drivers/ps4/ps4-fan.c | 278 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/ps4/ps4-fan.h |  37 ++++++
 3 files changed, 320 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/ps4/ps4-fan.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/ps4/ps4-fan.h

diff --git a/drivers/ps4/Makefile b/drivers/ps4/Makefile
index 11162a26055db432fb6652952dec18460cf108d4..e4728125d394a5fd9d38e6a22fceafce73867291 100644
--- a/drivers/ps4/Makefile
